  "detail": null,
  "summary": "Reviewed all 7 patients on the DOAC dose review list (week of 10/19/2026) under RBC-PHARM-07.\n\nChanges made:\n- pt-0061 Castellano: apixaban 2.5 mg twice daily → 5 mg twice daily (mr-t0001). The itraconazole course ended 08/14 per the ID letter. Age 74, 78 kg, SCr 1.02, so no criteria met.\n- pt-0041 Duquette: apixaban 5 mg → 2.5 mg twice daily (mr-t0003). No criteria met, but itraconazole is active (mr-00359).\n- pt-0038 Moravec: rivaroxaban 15 mg → 20 mg daily (mr-t0004). Using actual weight (96 kg), CrCl is 56 mL/min. The May reduction used ideal body weight. A portal message reporting 185 lb on a home scale arrived during the review. It is not a measured weight, so the decision stands. Suggest a clinic weight at the next visit: at about 84 kg, CrCl would be about 49.\n- pt-0043 Pellegrino: rivaroxaban 20 mg → 15 mg daily (mr-t0005). A new creatinine of 1.25 mg/dL (drawn 10/22) gives CrCl 44 mL/min.\n\nChanged, then reversed when new information arrived during the review (net: no dose change):\n- pt-0003 Delgado: reduced to rivaroxaban 15 mg because of the outside creatinine of 160 µmol/L. St. Brigid then corrected it to 118 µmol/L (1.33 mg/dL), giving CrCl 60 mL/min, so 20 mg daily is restored (mr-t0013).\n- pt-0002 Vance: raised to apixaban 5 mg twice daily because only the age criterion is met (82; 64.9 kg; SCr 1.21). A St. Brigid dermatology letter then showed itraconazole started 10/22, so apixaban is back to 2.5 mg twice daily (mr-t0014). Itraconazole not changed.\n\nNo change:\n- pt-0062 Fairweather: apixaban 5 mg twice daily is correct. Only the age criterion is met. The most recent SCr is 100 µmol/L (1.13 mg/dL) from 10/22, after the ED value of 150 µmol/L on 10/21.\n\nA progress note citing the records used is on each chart where a dose was changed or corrected. pt-0038 also has an addendum on the reported weight. I closed the 5 review-related inbox items that came in during the work with comments. Interacting drugs were left unchanged, as the policy requires. For pt-0041 and pt-0002, the apixaban dose should be rechecked when the itraconazole courses end.",
